[Music]  tight security protests  awkward group photos and some even more  awkward handshakes  you did very well last night my god that  was a difficult one they are the  familiar  features of these annual meetings of  global leaders  what actually is the g7  well it stands for the group of seven  but it started out life  as the group of six formed in 1975  france germany italy japan the us and  the uk  were the initial members the g6 became  the g7  in 1976 when canada joined and then it  became the g8 in 1998  with post-soviet union russia welcomed  into the club  now you might be thinking hang on a  second why all of a sudden  is it g7 again well in 2014  russia was kicked out in response to its  annexation of crimea from ukraine  g7 leaders taken in turns to hold the  presidency  each year and whoever is the president  hosts the meeting  and broadly speaking sets the agenda  the leaders spend a couple of days in a  luxury hotel  in a remote location holding meetings  and press conferences  then they try and agree what's called a  joint  communique a statement setting out their  position  on things like climate change counter  extremism  or confronting global health challenges  like malaria or aids  well the short answer is no indeed in  recent years disagreement and disunity  have defined proceedings far more than  unity  that was in no small part down to this  guy at the 2018 summit in canada donald  trump arrived late  and left early he had a row with other  leaders over trade tariffs and his  desire for russia to be readmitted but i  think it's much more appropriate to have  russia in  it should be the g8 because a lot of the  things we talk about  have to do with russia he ended up  withdrawing his support for the joint  communique  now although the official member list is  currently limited to seven countries  the invite list is a bit bigger than  that leaders of other nations  often join with australia spain and  india regularly in attendance  as well as the president of the eu  commission but there are questions about  whether the g7 ought to be  more inclusive particularly when it  comes to representatives from  african and latin american countries for  that reason  the g20 is rising in prominence it's not  been around for as long  and is more focused on issues like  markets and finance rather than wider  politics  but its membership includes the major  emerging economies  of brazil india mexico south africa  and not least china many analysts  suggest that while the g7  still sets the agenda for the global  discussion  increasingly it's the g20 where the real  business gets done

